Description:

The xtext escapes in an LMTP "MAIL FROM ... AUTH=" parameter now decode
correctly.  Previously each escape decoded to a NUL byte, truncating the
identity at the first one.  That identity is used for ACL checks and is
recorded in the Received: header, so a truncated identity could both
misattribute a delivery and change the authorization applied to it.

Cyrus listens for LMTP on a Unix domain socket by default, so only deployments
that have configured lmtpd to listen on a network socket were reachable by
anything other than a local process.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-6php-j5qr-hf4r.


